# Fixture: the ruler at two rounds — the paired df N - 1 puts t at 12.706, and h = t * sd / sqrt(N)
# with the default sd sqrt(2) x 0.6 % (both arms' same-binary 0.6 % in quadrature) is
# 12.706 * 0.6 * sqrt(2) / sqrt(2) = 12.706 * 0.6 = 7.624 %: a two-round sitting reads nothing
# smaller (the two-sample 4.303 at df 2 under-predicted this by ~3x).
kind: ab
question: does the fixture lever shorten the decode step?
term: decode tok/s @ n=96, depth 6, A6000 — (changed − base) / base, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +8..+12
rounds: 2
condition: both arms alternate in one lease, the order rotated every round; no row carries [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]
decide-in: land the lever
decide-below: keep it off and find the wrong term before another A/B
decide-above: land it and re-derive the term the model overstated
